  "description": "The applicant seeks to add a second-floor rear extension, with a third-floor roof terrace positioned above. An internal reconfiguration is proposed to facilitate the rear extension, which will accommodate a Therapy Room with an accessible ensuite shower room. It is important to note that the applicant has significant medical considerations that have influenced the design.\n\nIn response to these needs, the applicant has incorporated inclusive design features, including the installation of a stairlift with a tip-up seat, providing access to the upper floor of their duplex apartment. The top floor will also include an accessible ensuite in the main bedroom. This bedroom will lead onto the proposed rear-facing roof terrace.\n\nGiven the applicant’s mobility requirements, the addition of the roof terrace will help create level access to amenity space, which would be lost due to the proposed rear extension and the displacement of the existing roof terrace. The roof terrace will be enclosed by metal railings and privacy screens to ensure both safety and privacy. Additionally, two new windows are proposed as part of the rear extension.",
